  "statement": "Given a **0-indexed** `m x n` integer matrix `matrix`, create a new **0-indexed** matrix called `answer`. Make `answer` equal to `matrix`, then replace each element with the value `-1` with the **maximum** element in its respective column.\n\nReturn _the matrix_ `answer`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n![](./assets/modify-the-matrix-1.png)\n```\nInput: matrix = [[1,2,-1],[4,-1,6],[7,8,9]]\nOutput: [[1,2,9],[4,8,6],[7,8,9]]\nExplanation: The diagram above shows the elements that are changed (in blue).\n- We replace the value in the cell [1][1] with the maximum value in the column 1, that is 8.\n- We replace the value in the cell [0][2] with the maximum value in the column 2, that is 9.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n![](./assets/modify-the-matrix-2.png)\n```\nInput: matrix = [[3,-1],[5,2]]\nOutput: [[3,2],[5,2]]\nExplanation: The diagram above shows the elements that are changed (in blue).\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `m == matrix.length`\n*   `n == matrix[i].length`\n*   `2 <= m, n <= 50`\n*   `-1 <= matrix[i][j] <= 100`\n*   The input is generated such that each column contains at least one non-negative integer.",
  "constraints": [
    "m == matrix.length",
    "n == matrix[i].length",
    "2 <= m, n <= 50",
    "-1 <= matrix[i][j] <= 100",
    "The input is generated such that each column contains at least one non-negative integer."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "matrix = [[1,2,-1],[4,-1,6],[7,8,9]]",
